            "branchId": 112385,
            "branchIds": [],
            "organizationName": "Graduate Economics Student Association",
            "organizationProfilePicture": "df0f4d9c-e53a-422b-80fd-f15ed98cc29b1f2d1b96-6e3c-4cc9-92c7-376e7c6c03f3.png",
            "organizationNames": [],
            "name": "GESA Qualifying Exam Roundtable",
            "description": "<p></p>\r\n<div>Having trouble balancing day-to-day studies with preparations for the qualifying exams this spring? We'd love to help with that in any way that we can. One of our annual traditions with GESA is hosting a &ldquo;roundtable&rdquo; (like a presenter panel, but much more informal) event to talk about these exams and some things that we have learned from it, as upper-level students who have gone through the experience just like all of you. So we invite you to attend and to come chat with us!</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>See below for the event details.</div>\r\n<div>&mdash;</div>\r\n<div><strong><u>WHEN:</u></strong>&nbsp;Tuesday, March 24,&nbsp;5:00 - 7:00 PM</div>\r\n<div><strong><u>WHERE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Simon Library (3rd floor), New Jersey Hall</div>\r\n<div><strong><u>WHAT:</u></strong>&nbsp;This event is hosted for the express purpose of giving all students taking the qualifiers a chance to have an open and honest dialogue with a mixture of upper-level students. Our goal is to help you feel more prepared as you decide which exams to take, and also as you decide <em>how</em>&nbsp;you want to prepare for the summer. Importantly, <em><u>GESA will be providing FREE FOOD to all attendees!</u></em></div>",
            "location": "Simon Library - NJ Hall",
            "startsOn": "2026-03-24T21:00:00+00:00",
