            "organizationName": "Academic Programs at Douglass Residential College - DRC",
            "organizationProfilePicture": "5ed5910e-a369-4630-978c-8b9b350e348f9ba332eb-d00f-45f8-9203-7f07d1b096ab.png",
            "organizationNames": [],
            "name": "Needlepoint Workshop with artist Liz Collins ",
            "description": "<p>Join the Center for Women in the Arts at Douglass for a workshop led by acclaimed artist Liz Collins!</p>\r\n<p>This unique needlepoint workshop invites you to explore the meditative joy of stitching. Collins will guide participants through the myriad of stitches possible within needlepoint and share her distinctive methodology for creating improvisational designs, treating needlepoint as a slow drawing process in response to the grid.&nbsp;All skill levels and forms of stitching are welcome and supported.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Only open to Douglass and Art &amp; Design students.</strong> <br />Free supplies and snacks provided! Supplies/snacks are limited &ndash; First come, first served. Space is limited. Please arrive on-time.</p>\r\n<p><br />This experience counts towards the Douglass Discovery curriculum requirement. R3: Career/Discovery/Professional Development/Research. Reminder: To receive DRC curriculum credit, you must complete a <a href=\"https://rutgers.ca1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_3q7I2bGe7JIhYZE\">reflection survey</a>.</p>\r\n<p><br />*Liz Collins is the 2025-2026 Estelle Lebowitz &amp; Ann Beneduce-Lebowitz Artist-in-Residence. Her solo exhibition, <em>Shapeshifter</em>, is on view through March 13, 2026 in the Mary H. Dana Women Artists Series Galleries at Douglass Libraries.</p>\r\n<p>___</p>\r\n<p>* Image and Media Release<br />By attending this event, you acknowledge and agree that Rutgers University may photograph, record, or otherwise capture your artwork, image, and/or voice. You grant Rutgers the unrestricted right to use, reproduce, publish, and distribute these sound, still, or moving images in any medium for educational, promotional, advertising, or other purposes aligned with the University&rsquo;s mission. All rights to these materials will belong to Rutgers University. Please let our photographer or videographer know if you do not want your image taken at the event.</p>",
            "location": "Ludwig Center, Albers-Schonberg Rm",
