            "name": "Afrobeat Beyond the Grammys: Fela Kuti and Contemporary African Creativity",
            "description": "<p>Fela Kuti's posthumous Grammy recognition marks a milestone for African innovation. This panel of publicly engaged scholars illuminates the women who shaped his world--from feminist icon Funmilayo Ransome-Kuti to the collaborators and performers who sustained the Afrobeat movement across generations.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The event will start with a panel discussion featuring guests Jad Abumrad, Dr. Dotun Ayobade, Kehinde Alonge, and Dr. Judith Byfield.&nbsp;Jad Abumra is the host of the 12-part 2025 podcast series&nbsp;Fela Kuti: Fear No Man, exploring the life of the Afrobeat pioneer.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Afterwards, there will be a reception with live music played by DJ AK-47.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div data-ogsc=\"black\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Co-Sponsored by the Center for African Studies, English Department, Women and Gender Studies, and AMESALL.</div>\r\n<div data-ogsc=\"black\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div data-ogsc=\"black\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div data-ogsc=\"black\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Come learn and socialize in the Livingston Student Center Gathering Lounge!</div>",
